# These fixtures ARE their bytes. The root .gitattributes normalizes every
# file to LF (`* text=auto eol=lf`), which is right for source and wrong here:
# f04-crlf-bom exists to pin that a CRLF config.toml comes back CRLF, and with
# normalization on, git stored it as LF (54 bytes instead of 56) so the test
# compared LF input against LF expected -- green, and testing nothing. The
# same normalization on a Windows checkout would push CRLF onto the LF
# fixtures and break the ones that assert LF.
#
# `-text` turns the conversion off in both directions: what is committed is
# what lands in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# src/tests/client-config-toml.test.ts asserts the CRLF fixture still holds a
# CRLF and the LF fixtures still hold none, so if this file ever stops
# applying, a test says so instead of quietly passing.
* -text
